A||N||5||FieroSTETZ||finally had a chance to enter a road rally!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||04-11-2001||11:31 AM||||well, the family beater (1987 mazda 626 turbo w/ rally edition upgrades) went out and did a bit o rally drivin last night.. whooooo wheee! thats so much fun! i don't remember a time when i wasn't drifting around sideways! i am proud of the little @#!%box, because it beat the poo outta most of the competition (impreza wasn't so hot!) the details on the mazda are 2.0i 2 liter sohc 4 cylinder, toyota celica all trac turbocharger (the mazda one crapped out) and rally suspension, slight suspension lift, and a steel belly plate to protect the engine and gas tank and stuff. this car is so much fun! i used to offroad following my buddy in his 4x4 toyota pickup. he could climb over rocks better, but other than that i could almost always stick with him. sorry about the long post, i am all amped still! will try to post pics, sounds, and maybe some video if i can find the webspace||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||04-11-2001||01:42 PM||||Cool! How did you do the suspension lift? If I ever get ahead of the game enough to bring my 323 GTX up to snuff, I'd lke to put a lift on it. For some reason, Mazdas make very fun off-roaders for passenger cars.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSTETZ||04-12-2001||03:10 AM||||i wish i could find a 323 gtx around here - ever since you mentioned yours a long time ago, i researched and have been lookig for a good one around me, but have found NOTHING 323 with a turbo OR all wheel drive... fwd is fun in the 626, the 323 oughta be awesome. you ever had it to a track? anyways, i went to an off road truck place and the guy looked at the car, and pretty much kept the car for the day to find something that fits. its an auto (bummer!) but its kinda like selec shift or tiptronic, you can tickle the gears manually, has a 4 speed auto - bulletproof trans! 2nd engine, almost time for a third, and still the original trans, no rebuilds! any other fun little turbo cars i can maybe find that would be cool rally cars or itty bitty road warriors?||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||04-12-2001||10:49 AM||||Nope, never taken it to a track, but back in central CA, we had lots of farm roads and levy roads to go balls out on. Driving sideways at 70 mph in dirt is textbook definition of a rush!  ||||reg||1
